## Usage

```bash
# Initialize with S3 backend
terraform init \
  -backend-config="bucket=my-tfstate" \
  -backend-config="key=infra" \
  -backend-config="region=us-east-1" \
  -backend-config="encrypt=true"

# Deploy dev
terraform workspace new dev
terraform plan  -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars -out=dev.tfplan
terraform apply dev.tfplan

# Deploy prod (separate workspace = separate state)
terraform workspace new prod
terraform plan  -var-file=environments/prod.tfvars -out=prod.tfplan
terraform apply prod.tfplan
```

---

## Acceptance Criteria Mapping

| Criterion | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Bucket**: versioning, encryption, no public access | `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, `aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration`, `aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block` — all four blocks set to `true` |
| **RDS**: deletion protection, backup retention ≥ 7d, not public | `deletion_protection = true`, `backup_retention_period = 7/14`, `publicly_accessible = false` |
| **Secret**: never plaintext in Git | `random_password` generated at apply time, stored in `aws_secretsmanager_secret_version`, marked `sensitive` in variables |
| **IAM**: least privilege, no wildcards on prod | Prod policy actions explicitly enumerated; resources scoped to specific ARNs; OIDC trust for IRSA |
| **Environment isolation** | Terraform workspaces provide separate state files; `dev.tfvars` / `prod.tfvars` control sizing; `local.is_prod` gates prod-only resources |
